#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Step 03 Advertise: each node's commitment is published, fetched back, and verified.

Usage: 03-advertise --population DIR --out DIR

For every rehearsal node in DIR/population.json this signs the node's
commitment (steps/03-advertise.md) with the node's test key, publishes it to the first carrier,
a file in nodes/commitments/ of a git repository, reads it back from that
repository's HEAD with `git show`, and verifies the bytes it read back with
scripts/check_commitment.py: the fields, no counts, the signature under the
SPKI key, the policy digest against the policy bytes, the staple's and the
checkpoint's digests. Either commitment profile verifies: evidence-commitment/0
(one stapled card) or /1 (one card per evidence stream); the record names each
stapled card's stream (scripts/history_cards.py).

- rehearsal: the carrier is a scratch git repository (the repository's own
  nodes/ list holds no rehearsal node); it is kept as carrier.bundle, a proof
  file, so `git show` can be re-run on exactly what was fetched. On the Goose
  rehearsal population (scripts/goose_rehearsal.py), each node's commitment is
  the one the node signed itself with G1's loop_advertise, published byte for
  byte; the harness signs nothing, and the commitment must be under the node's
  own key.
- live: the harness never signs for a live node. A live commitment is one the
  node signed and published itself; the pinned capsules plugin signs and serves
  it (capsules-plugin PR #75, in the pin) and hands it to its operator, who
  adds it here by pull request. This reads the carrier's HEAD (--carrier,
  default this repository), publishes nothing, and requires the commitment to
  be under the key_id the list holds for that node. A node with no commitment
  there yet is NOT_CHECKED: nobody has published it (LIVE_GAP). It collects first
  (collect_live: carrier.json holds the carrier's HEAD commit and, per node, the
  listed key_id and which paths HEAD held; each commitment and policy is copied
  beside it) and then judges only those files (judge_live), so step 08 runs the
  same judge on the proof (loop#188).

Second carrier (loop#305): a rehearsal node with advertise/<name>/nostr.json (recorded relay responses) is also
read back from its Nostr announce event; the event's octets must equal the git carrier's bytes
(scripts/nostr_carrier.py, steps/03-advertise.md "The second carrier: Nostr"). A node without one is reported
"not advertised on nostr", not failed. The live read-back waits on Mesh-LLM/capsules-plugin#212.

Per-node inputs come from DIR/advertise/<name>/ (commitment.json,
history_card.json, checkpoint.json) when present. Without them a rehearsal
node gets stand-ins, named as such in the finding. The stapled history_card/1 is
verified by the pinned capsule-cli (`capsulectl verify --history`, scripts/staple_verify.py, installed by
steps/capsule-cli.setup.sh) under the node key and each card entry's checkpoint_key: a failing property fails the
node, a stand-in staple (the harness builds an evidence-commitment/0, loop#407), a missing binary or an entry
without a checkpoint_key (allowed, never refused here) leaves the card not checked. The
checkpoint attestation is not verified here (step 02 owns it). An evidence-commitment/0 is not run (capsule-cli takes no
keys for it). Each is a sentence in detail on a PASS when not
verified, otherwise a not_checked entry.
"""
